    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75796" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖθαρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, prop. of animals, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>udder</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.440
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				8.42
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				69
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθιέναι τὸ οὖθαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					523a1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ οὔθατα</span> distd. from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μαστοί</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.496c
			</span></i>; eaten as a dish, ib.<i><span class="en">
